{"name":"Lime Parfait","hex":"#95c577","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"lime","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["Any inorganic material containing calcium, usually calcium oxide (quicklime) or calcium hydroxide (slaked lime).","Any gluey or adhesive substance that traps or captures; sometimes a synonym for birdlime."]},{"part":"Verb","definitions":["To treat with calcium hydroxide or calcium oxide (lime).","To smear with birdlime.\n To ensnare, catch, entrap."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/lime"},{"term":"parfait","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A French parfait (parfait glacé), an iced dessert made with egg yolks, sugar, cream, and flavouring (usually fruit), sometimes with the addition of a liqueur.","An American parfait, a layered dessert often consisting of fruit, ice cream, pastries, whipped topping, etc. and served in a glass, often a parfait glass."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/parfait"}],"entries":[{"title":"Parfait","blocks":[{"text":"Parfait is either of two types of dessert. In France, where the dish originated, parfait is made by boiling cream, egg, sugar and syrup to create a custard-like or meringue-like puree which is then frozen. The American version consists of layers differentiated by the inclusion of such ingredients as granola, nuts, yogurt and liqueurs, topped off with fruits or whipped cream."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/7/73/Parfait_samples_by_pinguino_in_Osaka%2C_Japan.jpg/330px-Parfait_samples_by_pinguino_in_Osaka%2C_Japan.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Parfait","wikidata":"Q13314"},{"title":"Lime (color)","blocks":[{"text":"Lime is a color that is a shade of yellow-green, so named because it is a representation of the color of the citrus fruit lime. It is the color that is in between the web color chartreuse and yellow on the color wheel. Alternate names for this color included yellow-green, lemon-lime, lime green, or bitter lime."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/c/c2/AosaHGkyuai_%28cropped%29_3.jpg/330px-AosaHGkyuai_%28cropped%29_3.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Lime_(color)","wikidata":"Q906936"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/13/Parfait_glac%C3%A9_au_Grand_Marnier%2C_fruits_confits_et_pain_d%27%C3%A9pice.JPG/500px-Parfait_glac%C3%A9_au_Grand_Marnier%2C_fruits_confits_et_pain_d%27%C3%A9pice.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/13/Parfait_glac%C3%A9_au_Grand_Marnier%2C_fruits_confits_et_pain_d%27%C3%A9pice.JPG/1280px-Parfait_glac%C3%A9_au_Grand_Marnier%2C_fruits_confits_et_pain_d%27%C3%A9pice.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/13/Parfait_glac%C3%A9_au_Grand_Marnier%2C_fruits_confits_et_pain_d%27%C3%A9pice.JPG/500px-Parfait_glac%C3%A9_au_Grand_Marnier%2C_fruits_confits_et_pain_d%27%C3%A9pice.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"French parfait","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AParfait_glac%C3%A9_au_Grand_Marnier%2C_fruits_confits_et_pain_d'%C3%A9pice.JPG"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/4/49/Resort_Hotel_Olivean_Shodoshima_Japan11s5.jpg/500px-Resort_Hotel_Olivean_Shodoshima_Japan11s5.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/4/49/Resort_Hotel_Olivean_Shodoshima_Japan11s5.jpg/1280px-Resort_Hotel_Olivean_Shodoshima_Japan11s5.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/4/49/Resort_Hotel_Olivea